      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: toggles are pain to use compared to just simple click of button, gesture lock on controller for me was one of best thing about using index in vrchat, it allows to be much more expressive, especially when you have gestures that combine with each other/require 2 hands (tho it was a bit hard to activate it if both hands were using gesture that require not using thumb, as you needed to click very fast, that could be improved a bit by adding some additional super small delay, like max half a second).\nAction menu with toggles is nice for more advanced stuff, but for normal expressions during talks and running around the maps the gestures are just much more natural, and having a lock was making them twice as good. I could recommend people buying index just to get that single feature, and now its gone D:\nAlso... arent gestures just 2 number parameters in animator? lock can just set it to current value, I don't see how it makes it tough concept. No one will care if your own animation will change the gesture somehow, its only about preventing hands from changing current value.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
